      "problem": "Express $2\\sqrt{3}{cos}^{2}⁡{12}^{∘}-\\sqrt{3}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      "worked_solution": "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}(2{cos}^{2}⁡{12}^{∘}-1)\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={12}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}⁡{12}^{∘}-1 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {12}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}(2{cos}^{2}⁡{12}^{∘}-1) & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
